WEBVTT

00:48.851 --> 00:50.818
What are you
doing over there?

00:50.853 --> 00:52.486
I'm on hold
with tech support.

00:52.521 --> 00:53.821
My computer locked up
right in the middle

00:53.856 --> 00:55.155
of this story
I'm working on.

00:55.191 --> 00:57.524
God, even Microsoft Word
hates your writing.

00:57.560 --> 00:59.526
Thank you
for holding. How can I help you?

00:59.562 --> 01:02.529
Well, for starters, you can keep
talking with that lovely accent.

01:02.565 --> 01:05.532
Amazing. One second of a
stranger's voice on a phone

01:05.568 --> 01:07.534
and you've got
full Bollywood.

01:07.570 --> 01:09.870
I... I assume
she's in India.

01:09.905 --> 01:10.871
Your friend is correct.

01:10.906 --> 01:12.206
I am in India.

01:12.241 --> 01:14.541
But you sound like
a perfect gentleman to me.

01:14.577 --> 01:15.876
My name is Padma.

01:15.911 --> 01:17.878
Padma. That was
my mother's name.

01:17.913 --> 01:20.047
I'm gonna get
an English muffin.

01:20.082 --> 01:21.715
So what seems to be the problem?

01:21.751 --> 01:23.384
Well, one problem I have

01:23.419 --> 01:25.052
is that I have too much money.

01:25.087 --> 01:27.054
Then why don't you just
buy a new computer?

01:27.089 --> 01:28.389
What? I-I...

01:28.424 --> 01:30.391
Oh, I'm just
bursting your balls.

01:30.426 --> 01:31.725
Oh!

01:31.761 --> 01:33.727
Well, you're a feisty one.

01:33.763 --> 01:35.396
Uh, actually, my computer froze

01:35.431 --> 01:37.064
right in the middle
of a story I'm writing.

01:37.099 --> 01:38.399
Oh, you are a writer?

01:38.434 --> 01:39.733
Are you famous?

01:39.769 --> 01:41.235
By choice, no. No.

01:41.270 --> 01:43.570
Sometimes fame brings
a lot of unwanted attention.

01:43.606 --> 01:45.406
I mean, look at
William Shakespeare.

01:45.441 --> 01:47.408
William Shakespeare.
Aye.

01:47.443 --> 01:48.676
Nice collar,
you fruit.

01:48.711 --> 01:49.677
Thank ye.

01:49.712 --> 01:50.744
Hey, Shakespeare.

01:50.780 --> 01:52.413
What's the title
of your next play?

01:52.448 --> 01:55.082
<i>You should call it
Homosexual Collar Guy.</i>

01:55.117 --> 01:57.751
Ah, thy japes and jabs cut me
to the quick, squire.

01:57.787 --> 01:59.086
What does that
even mean?

01:59.121 --> 02:00.087
I know.

02:00.122 --> 02:01.755
It means, "I use
this collar as a bib

02:01.791 --> 02:03.424
for when I
service guys."

02:03.459 --> 02:05.125
Thank ye, thank ye.

02:07.763 --> 02:09.129
So, how'd you
like the collar?

02:09.165 --> 02:11.165
'Tis not for me.

02:17.807 --> 02:19.440
Huh, there's no one there.

02:19.475 --> 02:20.941
Must have been
some kids knocking.

02:20.976 --> 02:22.276
Down here, Lois.

02:22.311 --> 02:24.278
Oh, for God's
sake, Joe.

02:24.313 --> 02:26.947
Can't you put a tall flag on the
back of your chair or something?

02:26.982 --> 02:30.951
I apologize for the difficulty
my paralysis causes you.

02:30.986 --> 02:32.720
Hey, Peter. Good news.

02:32.755 --> 02:34.722
Bonnie's out of town,
so I have an extra ticket

02:34.757 --> 02:37.725
for Tuesday night bingo
down at the Allendale Mill.

02:37.760 --> 02:39.393
Why the hell would I
want to go to bingo?

02:39.428 --> 02:40.728
Oh, it's a blast.

02:40.763 --> 02:43.397
There's the thrill of the game,
people bring snacks,

02:43.432 --> 02:45.733
plus you'll hear some
pretty unfiltered opinions

02:45.768 --> 02:47.735
about those jokers
in Washington.

02:47.770 --> 02:49.870
Yeah, that sounds
perfectly terrible.

02:49.905 --> 02:51.205
You know what, Joe?

02:51.240 --> 02:52.873
Peter would love
to go with you.

02:52.908 --> 02:54.208
What?!
Terrific.

02:54.243 --> 02:56.110
I'll pick you up at 6:00.

02:56.145 --> 02:57.444
What'd you do that for?!

02:57.480 --> 02:58.779
Peter, he's your friend.

02:58.814 --> 03:00.781
Who knows?
It might be fun.

03:00.816 --> 03:02.449
All right, I'll go.

03:02.485 --> 03:03.784
But I'm not happy.

03:03.819 --> 03:06.286
You know how much I hate
being told what to do.

03:17.500 --> 03:19.767
You know, Padma,
I love Indian food.

03:19.802 --> 03:22.603
But I'd have to say my least
favorite curry is Ann.

03:23.806 --> 03:25.773
She's... she's
a newscaster here.

03:25.808 --> 03:27.775
I... I wish I could have
slipped that in earlier.

03:27.810 --> 03:29.109
Oh, no, I know her.

03:29.145 --> 03:31.111
She's internationally despised.

03:31.147 --> 03:33.113
So, are you done rebooting?

03:33.149 --> 03:35.449
Look, uh,
I have to come clean.

03:35.484 --> 03:38.786
Um, my computer wasn't
actually broken this time.

03:38.821 --> 03:41.121
Uh, I just wanted
to talk to you again.

03:41.157 --> 03:43.157
I like talking
to you, too, Brian.

03:43.192 --> 03:45.492
Oh, hey, is that Padma
from tech support again?

03:45.528 --> 03:46.493
Yeah. Yeah, it is.

03:46.529 --> 03:48.162
Oh, cool.
Ask her a question for me.

03:48.197 --> 03:50.497
How come over there
they just talk on the phone,

03:50.533 --> 03:51.832
and over here
they're all doctors?

03:51.867 --> 03:53.507
Get out of here. Lois
said you're supposed

03:53.536 --> 03:55.176
to sit on the potty
for one hour straight.

03:55.204 --> 03:56.837
I'm taking a break.
I got bored.

03:56.872 --> 03:58.772
And you've been on the phone
for more than an hour.

03:58.808 --> 04:00.274
I'm sorry.
Can you give me a sec?

04:00.309 --> 04:01.608
Look, I know it's crazy,

04:01.644 --> 04:03.610
but I honestly feel
a connection to this woman.

04:03.646 --> 04:05.846
More than I have
to anyone in a long time.

04:05.881 --> 04:08.182
That's nice, Brian, but
you're from different worlds.

04:08.217 --> 04:09.183
She's in India.

04:09.218 --> 04:10.317
That's a lot to overcome.

04:10.352 --> 04:11.985
People in love can
overcome anything.

04:12.021 --> 04:13.320
I guess you're right.

04:13.355 --> 04:15.689
I mean, look at
Jeb Bush and his wife.

04:15.724 --> 04:18.325
Honey, do you think
I'll ever be president?

04:18.360 --> 04:21.462
No, no, no.

04:21.497 --> 04:22.463
Stewie!

04:22.498 --> 04:23.630
What? It's just a joke.

04:23.666 --> 04:24.798
Yeah, but come on.

04:24.834 --> 04:26.133
Look it up, man.
Google her.

04:26.168 --> 04:28.235
I know what
she looks like.

04:33.342 --> 04:36.310
Oh, I see you came
with the Big Cheese.

04:36.345 --> 04:37.311
What?

04:37.346 --> 04:38.312
You?

04:38.347 --> 04:39.646
You're the Big Cheese?

04:39.682 --> 04:40.981
I usually bring
a variety wheel

04:41.016 --> 04:42.649
of Laughing Cow cheese.

04:42.685 --> 04:44.985
Laughing Cow!

04:45.020 --> 04:47.054
That's got to be
a happy farm, right?

04:48.791 --> 04:50.757
Oh, you just must be
cracking up all the time

04:50.793 --> 04:52.426
hanging out
with this one.

04:52.461 --> 04:54.761
Look, ma'am, I don't know
what signals Joe is sending out,

04:54.797 --> 04:55.996
but I'm married.

04:56.031 --> 04:58.665
G-49.

04:58.701 --> 05:01.001
Hey, and you're
already on the board.

05:01.036 --> 05:02.669
You're a natural at this.

05:02.705 --> 05:06.006
Oh, and fair warning,
when they call O-69,

05:06.041 --> 05:10.010
I say, "Oh, my! Ooh-la-la!"

05:11.380 --> 05:12.679
Yeah, really
funny, Joe.

05:12.715 --> 05:14.014
Or-or how about
this one?

05:14.049 --> 05:17.551
"Oh... my God, I want to
kill myself right now."

05:17.586 --> 05:18.886
All right, I got
to get through this.

05:18.921 --> 05:20.387
I'm just gonna go
to my happy place.

05:20.422 --> 05:22.055
Go to your happy place, Peter.

05:24.093 --> 05:27.461
Oh, and you're wearing
the necklace I gave you.

05:28.531 --> 05:30.931
Well, if I were you,
I'd sure be excited.

05:30.966 --> 05:33.267
You're only one number away
from having a bingo.

05:33.302 --> 05:34.268
I am?

05:34.303 --> 05:35.269
What, you mean
if they call...

05:35.304 --> 05:37.404
O-74.

05:38.741 --> 05:41.942
Bingo!

05:41.977 --> 05:43.944
You were right, Joe,
this is awesome.

05:43.979 --> 05:45.612
I've never won anything.

05:45.648 --> 05:48.215
Well, except for when I won
that "Tori Spelling Bee."

05:48.250 --> 05:51.785
Peter, your word is "equine."

05:51.820 --> 05:54.121
Peter reached this
round by accurately spelling

05:54.156 --> 05:57.925
"collagen," "repulsive"
and "botched."

06:01.463 --> 06:03.330
God, I can't believe
you're still at work, Padma.

06:03.365 --> 06:04.665
It's, like, 2:00 in the morning.

06:04.700 --> 06:05.999
No, it is noon here.

06:06.035 --> 06:07.501
Do you not know
about time zones?

06:07.536 --> 06:08.835
Oh, uh, yeah, oh, that's right.

06:08.871 --> 06:10.504
You guys are on metric.

06:10.539 --> 06:11.838
Oh, you're in here?

06:11.874 --> 06:13.173
Yeah, I'm on the phone.

06:13.208 --> 06:15.175
Is, uh, is Chris down
in the laundry room?

06:15.210 --> 06:16.343
Yeah, I think so.

06:16.378 --> 06:18.011
Okay, looks
like this is gonna be

06:18.047 --> 06:20.013
a stander-upper
in the garage.

06:20.049 --> 06:21.014
Uh-oh, six percent.

06:21.050 --> 06:22.149
Better hustle.

06:22.184 --> 06:24.151
It's so nice to talk
to you, Brian.

06:24.186 --> 06:25.819
You make me feel wonderful.

06:25.854 --> 06:27.821
God, if only you
weren't so far away.

06:27.856 --> 06:29.823
I wish I could just somehow
magically appear there

06:29.858 --> 06:31.158
and meet you in person.

06:31.193 --> 06:33.827
Oh, Brian, that would
be like a dream.

06:33.862 --> 06:34.828
Okay, I should go.

06:34.863 --> 06:36.830
I have 11,000 people on hold.

06:36.865 --> 06:38.498
Good-bye, Padma.

06:38.534 --> 06:39.833
What the hell's
going on?

06:39.868 --> 06:41.168
Somebody's screaming
in the garage.

06:41.203 --> 06:42.502
Why are you still up?

06:42.538 --> 06:43.837
Because I'm in love.

06:43.872 --> 06:45.172
Oh, with that
Indian chick?

06:45.207 --> 06:46.506
What was her
name? Dot?

06:46.542 --> 06:48.175
No, it's not Dot,
it's Padma.

06:48.210 --> 06:50.010
And I have to be with her.

06:50.045 --> 06:52.512
Stewie, I'm going to India.

06:52.548 --> 06:54.181
Oh, my God,
I'm going with you.

06:54.216 --> 06:56.717
My yoga class will
be so jealous.

06:56.752 --> 06:59.386
Hey, everyone, the guy
I told you about, Brian,

06:59.421 --> 07:01.388
he's taking me to India!

07:01.423 --> 07:03.523
Oh, my God!

07:22.191 --> 07:23.824
We finally made
it, Brian.

07:23.859 --> 07:24.824
We're in India.

07:24.860 --> 07:26.826
Excuse me, man with no pupil,

07:26.862 --> 07:29.496
where can we get
a taxicab around here?

07:29.531 --> 07:30.830
All right,
let's do it, Stewie.

07:30.866 --> 07:32.165
Let's go find Padma.

07:32.200 --> 07:34.834
Shouldn't be hard in this
dreamy land of wonder.

07:34.871 --> 07:37.838
I can already smell the
enlightenment and tranquility.

07:44.980 --> 07:46.946
This is wonderful,
isn't it, Brian?

07:46.982 --> 07:48.648
It's so tranquil,
I'm tearing up.

07:48.683 --> 07:50.150
Come on, I think
I see a cab

07:50.185 --> 07:52.185
with less than
nine people in it.

07:57.392 --> 07:59.025
All right,
it's winning time.

07:59.060 --> 08:00.693
Let's get this show
on the road.

08:00.729 --> 08:02.362
After all, it's not
called "bing-stop,"

08:02.397 --> 08:04.364
it's called "bing-go!"

08:05.400 --> 08:06.699
That's very clever.

08:06.735 --> 08:08.701
Yeah, and, uh...
uh, maybe if I win,

08:08.737 --> 08:10.703
I'll yell, "bing-Joe."

08:10.739 --> 08:11.871
Don't force it, Joe.

08:11.907 --> 08:13.039
Yeah, be quiet, Joe.

08:13.074 --> 08:14.541
Me and the gang are trying
to hear our numbers.

08:14.576 --> 08:15.875
"You" and the gang?

08:15.911 --> 08:17.043
I'm the one who
brought you here.

08:17.078 --> 08:18.211
Yeah, well, you
know something?

08:18.246 --> 08:19.879
<i>The Mayflower also
brought fungus,</i>

08:19.915 --> 08:21.548
which then became
the Potato Famine.

08:21.583 --> 08:23.216
What the hell are
you talking about?

08:23.251 --> 08:24.717
I don't know, I've had,
like, four Ensures.

08:24.753 --> 08:26.052
I'm out of my mind.

08:26.087 --> 08:28.721
Peter, I brought you here
to have fun, not take over.

08:28.757 --> 08:30.390
Look, Joe, I'm a
little busy right now,

08:30.425 --> 08:32.725
<i>so I'm gonna have the Somali
pirate from Captain Phillips</i>

08:32.761 --> 08:34.060
tell you something.

08:34.095 --> 08:36.062
Joe, look at me.

08:36.097 --> 08:37.730
Look at me.

08:37.766 --> 08:39.766
He is the bingo captain now.

08:48.310 --> 08:50.276
I tell you, I love
it here, Brian.

08:50.312 --> 08:51.611
The sounds,
the colors.

08:51.646 --> 08:52.946
You know, this is
where the Beatles came

08:52.981 --> 08:54.280
to ruin their music.

08:54.316 --> 08:55.281
Yeah, yeah, that's great.

08:55.317 --> 08:56.416
Anyway, Padma works
in Bangalore,

08:56.451 --> 08:58.284
so we got to hurry
and catch the train.

08:58.320 --> 09:00.553
Can't believe
we're really in India.

09:00.589 --> 09:01.621
Oh, look over there.

09:01.656 --> 09:02.622
There's cute little
kids are playing

09:02.657 --> 09:04.424
Cowboys and Indians
and Indians.

09:04.459 --> 09:06.092
I'm gonna shoot you
with my six-gun.

09:06.127 --> 09:08.094
I'm gonna shoot you
with my bow and arrow.

09:08.129 --> 09:09.762
I'm just going to stand
here wearing a shirt

09:09.798 --> 09:11.598
that appears
to be a jacket.

09:19.241 --> 09:21.541
Do you think all those
chickens had to buy tickets?

09:21.576 --> 09:23.209
I don't know,
but I'm starving.

09:23.245 --> 09:25.945
What I wouldn't give right now
for a big juicy steak.

09:25.981 --> 09:27.113
How dare you?

09:27.148 --> 09:28.781
To us, cows
are sacred!

09:28.817 --> 09:30.783
That's right, you
are disrespecting

09:30.819 --> 09:32.118
our entire culture.

09:32.153 --> 09:35.421
And why did Wes Anderson come
here to make his worst movie?

09:35.457 --> 09:37.757
Stewie, what do we do?
Quick, hit the red buttons!

09:42.497 --> 09:44.130
Wow, that came in handy.
Yeah.

09:44.165 --> 09:45.965
Now let's get out of here.
Let's see what their wieners look like.

09:46.001 --> 09:47.634
Yeah. Yeah, no,
let's get out of here.

09:51.206 --> 09:53.172
Okay, I'm off to bingo.

09:53.208 --> 09:54.507
Peter, what are
you wearing?

09:54.543 --> 09:56.175
Oh, you mean
my bingo cape?

09:56.211 --> 09:57.844
That's our holiday
tablecloth.

09:57.879 --> 10:00.179
I'm sorry, Lois, but my
people have come to expect

10:00.215 --> 10:02.181
a certain degree of pageantry.

10:02.217 --> 10:03.516
Don't wait up.

10:03.552 --> 10:04.851
We may go to Denny's.

10:04.886 --> 10:06.286
Is Joe going with you?

10:06.321 --> 10:07.620
Oh, "Crybaby Joe"?

10:07.656 --> 10:08.955
Nah, he doesn't come anymore.

10:08.990 --> 10:10.623
I think he resents my skill.

10:10.659 --> 10:12.559
Peter, bingo was
Joe's favorite thing.

10:12.594 --> 10:14.627
Now, you go over there
and take him with you,

10:14.663 --> 10:15.962
or I don't want
you going at all.

10:15.997 --> 10:17.964
Hey, hey, hey, don't try
to take this away from me.

10:17.999 --> 10:19.966
This is the only thing
I've ever been good at.

10:20.001 --> 10:22.769
Well, this and timing
my farts to a thunderstorm.

10:22.804 --> 10:24.871
Why don't we all go ahead and
turn to page six in the handout?

10:24.906 --> 10:26.873
Ah...

10:26.908 --> 10:28.942
The first thing you're
gonna notice is a bar graph.

10:28.977 --> 10:31.644
And what that is is to indicate
our international sales,

10:33.214 --> 10:34.548
which peaked, of course,
- Oh, yeah.

10:34.573 --> 10:35.283
during the last quarter.

10:35.283 --> 10:37.417
But now we're expecting
that to drop off

10:37.452 --> 10:39.018
as we enter the
colder weather.

10:42.791 --> 10:44.824
The storm's moving away.

10:49.798 --> 10:50.830
We made it!

10:50.865 --> 10:52.198
This is where Padma works!

10:52.233 --> 10:55.835
I feel like I owe every bus
in America an apology.

10:58.206 --> 10:59.639
So, we haven't discussed
what you're going

10:59.674 --> 11:00.940
to do if she's a pig.

11:00.976 --> 11:02.342
She's already
beautiful to me.

11:02.377 --> 11:04.911
And you know,
we'll see.

11:13.722 --> 11:15.588
My God, how you
gonna find her?

11:15.624 --> 11:17.064
There are hundreds
of people in here.

11:17.092 --> 11:19.492
Don't worry, I
thought of that.

11:19.527 --> 11:20.827
Thank you
for calling tech support.

11:20.862 --> 11:21.995
How can I help you?

11:22.030 --> 11:23.030
I'll tell you how.

11:23.064 --> 11:24.297
Stand on your desk.

11:24.332 --> 11:25.332
Brian?

11:25.367 --> 11:26.666
Padma, just do it.

11:28.770 --> 11:29.836
Oh, boy.

11:29.871 --> 11:31.170
Are you Padma?

11:31.206 --> 11:32.739
No, I am Ranita.

11:32.774 --> 11:34.774
There is a python in my cube.

11:36.978 --> 11:38.578
Brian?

11:38.613 --> 11:39.545
Padma!

11:39.581 --> 11:40.747
I can't believe this!

11:40.782 --> 11:42.215
Why are you here?

11:42.250 --> 11:44.417
Because I was having
a technical issue

11:44.452 --> 11:45.852
with my heart.

11:45.887 --> 11:47.453
Ugh, 16 hours on a plane,

11:47.489 --> 11:49.288
<i>and that's what you
came up with?</i>

11:49.324 --> 11:51.691
I am touched you came
all this way to see me.

11:51.726 --> 11:53.326
I'm so glad I did.

11:53.361 --> 11:56.329
You're even more beautiful
than I imagined.

11:58.600 --> 12:00.933
Well, I have to admit
you two do make a cute couple.

12:00.969 --> 12:04.237
But then again, so did Chris
Martin and Gwyneth Paltrow.

12:04.272 --> 12:06.005
Do you take this woman
to lecture you

12:06.041 --> 12:08.708
about trans fats for as long
as you both shall live?

12:08.743 --> 12:09.976
I do.

12:10.011 --> 12:11.544
And do you take this man to be

12:11.579 --> 12:14.113
a watered-down Bono
until death do you part?

12:14.149 --> 12:15.448
I do.

12:15.483 --> 12:17.483
I now pronounce you
pretentious and terrible.

12:17.519 --> 12:20.486
You may name your daughter
after a fruit.

12:26.327 --> 12:27.660
So, this is my town.

12:27.696 --> 12:29.462
I have lived here
my whole life.

12:29.497 --> 12:31.998
Well, if you were born here,
then it must be a magical place.

12:32.033 --> 12:33.800
Yes, let's go get
sandwiches

12:33.835 --> 12:36.235
at that New Delhi
I keep hearing about.

12:37.772 --> 12:39.772
Thanks, Ganesha.

12:39.808 --> 12:42.008
I am so happy
that you are here.

12:42.043 --> 12:45.078
In fact, my family is
having a big party tonight.

12:45.113 --> 12:47.313
You must both come
as my guests.

12:47.348 --> 12:48.748
Oh, an Indian party!

12:48.783 --> 12:50.817
I hope they play that one song
with the shrieking, nasal,

12:50.852 --> 12:54.487
atonal woman over the bongos
and tambourines.

13:02.897 --> 13:04.063
You seem nervous.

13:04.099 --> 13:05.898
Are you worried
about meeting Padma's family?

13:05.934 --> 13:07.734
Yeah. Well, that,
and this is always

13:07.769 --> 13:09.469
<i>what it looks
like on Homeland</i>

13:09.504 --> 13:10.904
right before there's
a drone strike.

13:10.939 --> 13:13.673
Oh, my, you both
look so elegant.

13:13.708 --> 13:16.008
Thanks, I did a little
shopping today.

13:16.044 --> 13:17.477
Not me.
Mine is actually

13:17.512 --> 13:19.245
an Aladdin costume
from last Halloween.

13:19.280 --> 13:21.114
I never travel without it.

13:22.817 --> 13:24.083
Family, guests,

13:24.119 --> 13:26.886
and monkeys who have
wandered in to steal fruit,

13:26.921 --> 13:30.656
it is my honor to welcome you
to this engagement celebration.

13:30.692 --> 13:31.692
Oh, "engagement"?

13:31.726 --> 13:33.025
So, who's getting married?

13:33.061 --> 13:34.293
I am.

13:34.329 --> 13:36.129
What?!

13:36.164 --> 13:37.930
Padma, my beloved daughter.

13:37.966 --> 13:40.166
Dhiraj, my future son-in-law.

13:40.201 --> 13:42.468
Please, come
and meet one another.

13:42.504 --> 13:44.170
Welp, that's a Punjab
to the figs.

13:44.205 --> 13:46.038
Where's the bar?

13:47.475 --> 13:49.709
Everyone, you are all
so kind to come tonight,

13:49.744 --> 13:52.311
and it is so nice
to meet you, Dhiraj.

13:52.347 --> 13:56.082
But something happened today,
and I can no longer marry you.

13:56.117 --> 13:57.650
Padma, what is it?

13:57.685 --> 13:59.519
My true love is here tonight.

13:59.554 --> 14:01.921
He has come to me
all the way from America.

14:01.956 --> 14:04.190
His name is Brian Griffin.

14:04.225 --> 14:06.559
And my heart belongs to him.

14:09.531 --> 14:11.030
Quick, everyone's
looking at the dog!

14:11.065 --> 14:12.832
Go, go, go!

14:17.669 --> 14:20.036
Padma, you cannot
call off the wedding!

14:20.071 --> 14:23.373
I have already paid a large
dowry to Dhiraj's family!

14:23.408 --> 14:25.508
But it would be wrong
to marry someone I do not love.

14:25.544 --> 14:28.077
The one I love is Brian.

14:28.113 --> 14:30.980
Sir, what if I were to repay you
for all you've spent?

14:31.016 --> 14:33.716
Would Padma then be free
to marry whoever she wanted?

14:33.752 --> 14:34.951
Brian!

14:34.986 --> 14:36.085
You would do that?

14:36.121 --> 14:37.921
Yes.
I love you, Padma,

14:37.956 --> 14:40.223
and-and I'd do anything
to be with you.

14:40.258 --> 14:42.225
I suppose that
might be possible.

14:42.260 --> 14:44.127
Great, just give me
a chance to raise the money,

14:44.162 --> 14:46.095
so I can marry your daughter
and make her happy.

14:46.131 --> 14:48.965
Oh, so you don't
have the money?

14:49.000 --> 14:52.302
He's holding onto an Applebee's
gift card with $1.62 on it.

14:52.337 --> 14:54.070
I do not know
Applebee's.

14:54.105 --> 14:56.172
Is it like our
Colonel Chutney's?

14:56.208 --> 14:57.874
Does Colonel Chutney's
make you sick?

14:57.909 --> 14:59.008
Not every time.

14:59.044 --> 15:01.044
Then, no,
it's very different.

15:04.916 --> 15:06.716
I mean, my wife and I have
never said the words

15:06.751 --> 15:08.218
"open marriage," but...

15:08.253 --> 15:09.486
Oh, hey, Lois!

15:09.521 --> 15:11.187
Peter, it's time
to come home

15:11.223 --> 15:13.690
and give Joe back
his stupid little activity.

15:13.725 --> 15:15.758
I appreciate that,
Lois.

15:15.794 --> 15:16.960
First of all, this
is my favorite thing

15:16.995 --> 15:18.695
in the world now, so no.

15:18.730 --> 15:20.463
And second of all, we're
about to play a new round,

15:20.499 --> 15:21.764
so start taking
your pants off,

15:21.800 --> 15:23.333
'cause when I win,
I want you ready.

15:23.368 --> 15:24.901
Peter, if it wasn't for Joe,

15:24.936 --> 15:26.803
you wouldn't know
about bingo anyway.

15:26.838 --> 15:30.273
This meant everything to him,
and you've taken it away.

15:30.308 --> 15:32.442
As a friend, do the right thing

15:32.477 --> 15:35.245
and give Joe back
the happiness he found here.

15:41.353 --> 15:44.654
Joe, gag on my fat dauber.

15:45.957 --> 15:47.690
Damn it, I didn't want
to have to do this,

15:47.726 --> 15:49.325
but you've left
me no choice!

15:49.361 --> 15:51.194
Kids, get in here!

15:51.229 --> 15:52.795
Yay! Time with Dad!

15:52.831 --> 15:55.632
That's a bingo for me!

15:55.667 --> 15:57.400
All right,
how do you play?

15:57.435 --> 15:58.835
"Free space"?!

15:58.870 --> 16:00.703
Wow! What's that about?!

16:00.739 --> 16:02.105
I call I sit
next to Dad!

16:03.375 --> 16:04.541
All right, forget this.

16:04.576 --> 16:05.708
Let's all go home and each do

16:05.744 --> 16:07.744
our own individual media things.

16:13.885 --> 16:15.518
Stewie, I don't think
this is gonna work.

16:15.554 --> 16:16.986
We're never gonna
raise enough money

16:17.022 --> 16:18.621
to pay back
Padma's father.

16:18.657 --> 16:20.423
Trust me, Brian, there are
a billion people here,

16:20.458 --> 16:22.692
and almost every one
of them has a tapeworm.

16:22.727 --> 16:24.594
Yes, excuse me,
I have a tapeworm.

16:24.629 --> 16:26.396
All right, very good.
Lie down on your stomach.

16:26.431 --> 16:28.431
This won't hurt a bit.

16:34.706 --> 16:36.406
Hey, how are you guys?

16:36.441 --> 16:37.640
Oh, you're a lady.

16:37.676 --> 16:38.808
And you sound
American.

16:38.843 --> 16:40.209
How long have you
been in there?

16:40.245 --> 16:42.078
I originally just came
for my junior year,

16:42.113 --> 16:45.582
but I fell in love
with the place.

16:45.617 --> 16:47.350
Stewie, there's no way
I'm sitting here all day

16:47.385 --> 16:49.419
watching tapeworms
come out of butts.

16:49.454 --> 16:51.187
I'm doomed.

16:51.222 --> 16:53.523
I'll never be able
to pay for Padma's dowry.

16:53.558 --> 16:54.824
I don't understand.

16:54.859 --> 16:57.093
In movies, everything in India
always turns out great.

16:57.128 --> 16:59.929
Julia Roberts ate or loved
or prayed or something.

16:59.965 --> 17:01.664
I don't, I don't know.
I didn't see it.

17:01.700 --> 17:02.732
Wait a minute!

17:02.767 --> 17:04.400
Movies about India.

17:04.436 --> 17:06.836
I know how I can make the money!

17:08.773 --> 17:10.840
Who wants to be

17:10.875 --> 17:13.242
a millionaire?

17:14.613 --> 17:17.780
Our next contestant comes
all the way from America!

17:17.816 --> 17:20.750
Brian Griffin!

17:20.785 --> 17:22.685
What brings you to India, Brian?

17:22.721 --> 17:23.853
I'll tell you what brought me.

17:23.888 --> 17:25.021
True love.

17:25.056 --> 17:26.923
He's breaking up a marriage!

17:26.958 --> 17:30.693
All right, let's get started.

17:30.729 --> 17:33.696
First question--
"Which retired Indian cricketer

17:33.732 --> 17:35.865
"has scored over
18,000 runs

17:35.900 --> 17:37.767
in ODI competition?"

17:37.802 --> 17:39.502
Um, O...?
Wha...?

17:39.537 --> 17:41.771
O-ODI?
What?

17:41.806 --> 17:44.073
Is it A) Anil Kumble,

17:44.109 --> 17:46.976
B) Mahendra Singh Dhoni,

17:47.012 --> 17:49.979
C) Sachin Tendulkar,

17:50.015 --> 17:52.415
or D) Jiminy Cricket?

17:52.450 --> 17:55.451
Well, I know, I know
it's not Jiminy Cricket.

17:55.487 --> 17:58.655
Unless Jiminy's
based on a real person.

17:58.690 --> 17:59.889
I need an answer.

17:59.924 --> 18:00.923
You know, the more I say it,

18:00.959 --> 18:02.358
the more it does sound Indian.

18:02.394 --> 18:03.693
Jiminy Cricket.

18:03.728 --> 18:06.729
D) Jiminy Cricket, final answer.

18:09.100 --> 18:11.034
I'm sorry,
that is incorrect.

18:11.069 --> 18:12.502
Thank you for playing!

18:12.537 --> 18:13.836
We'll be right back

18:13.872 --> 18:16.506
after this message
from the Indian Census Bureau.

18:16.541 --> 18:17.607
Too many people!

18:17.642 --> 18:19.442
Stop with the people!

18:22.647 --> 18:24.013
Padma, I'm sorry.

18:24.049 --> 18:25.381
I still haven't
raised the money.

18:25.417 --> 18:26.649
But I'm working on it.

18:26.685 --> 18:28.084
There is no longer a need.

18:28.119 --> 18:29.752
My father has
solved the problem

18:29.788 --> 18:32.355
by promising Dhiraj
the hand of my younger sister.

18:32.390 --> 18:34.357
Oh, Padma, I meant
to ask you, are there, like,

18:34.392 --> 18:36.292
Bengal tigers just
running loose in the cities?

18:36.327 --> 18:37.627
I don't know.

18:37.662 --> 18:39.462
In America, are there
annoying talking babies

18:39.497 --> 18:40.997
always interrupting?

18:41.032 --> 18:42.999
Okay, it's been
a long trip.

18:43.034 --> 18:45.334
Let's not say anything
we're gonna regret.

18:45.370 --> 18:47.470
Wait a minute, so if,
if Dhiraj is marrying

18:47.505 --> 18:49.639
your sister, that means
we can be together!

18:49.674 --> 18:51.674
Actually, about that.

18:51.710 --> 18:54.477
I think watching you try to
answer that question out there,

18:54.512 --> 18:56.312
I realized something.

18:56.347 --> 18:58.548
You know nothing
of my country or my culture.

18:58.583 --> 19:00.483
Well, tha-that was a
really tough question.

19:00.518 --> 19:01.884
No, it wasn't.

19:01.920 --> 19:05.621
Everyone in India knows
who Sachin Tendulkar is.

19:05.657 --> 19:08.357
Brian, I am deeply touched
that you came all this way

19:08.393 --> 19:10.860
to find me,
but the truth is, you and I

19:10.895 --> 19:12.628
have very little in common.

19:12.664 --> 19:13.763
Well, I could learn!

19:13.798 --> 19:15.331
I mean, I mean,
there's got to be

19:15.366 --> 19:17.834
<i>an old Carmen Sandiego episode
on India or something.</i>

19:17.869 --> 19:20.069
Brian, Brian, punt, punt.

19:20.105 --> 19:21.771
I know you would try,
Brian.

19:21.806 --> 19:23.239
But when I look
inside myself,

19:23.274 --> 19:25.641
I realize I do not
want to marry you.

19:25.677 --> 19:28.277
Mostly, I just did not
want to marry Dhiraj.

19:28.313 --> 19:30.213
I am so sorry.

19:30.248 --> 19:33.182
Have I answered all of your
questions to your satisfaction?

19:33.218 --> 19:35.451
No! I came halfway
around the world for you!

19:35.487 --> 19:37.086
You said I was your true love!

19:37.122 --> 19:38.554
Well, by coming here,

19:38.590 --> 19:40.990
you saved me from a lifetime
of unhappiness.

19:41.025 --> 19:44.026
And I will always
love you for that.

19:44.062 --> 19:46.062
Good-bye, Brian.

19:48.133 --> 19:50.166
A peck on the cheek?

19:50.201 --> 19:52.535
Was that worth
an $8,000 coach ticket?

19:52.570 --> 19:53.803
You know what?

19:53.838 --> 19:55.638
It's about the journey,
not the destination.

19:55.673 --> 19:56.939
No, it's not.

19:56.975 --> 19:58.641
This sucked
and you failed.

19:58.676 --> 19:59.709
Story over!

19:59.744 --> 20:01.043
Bollywood!

20:05.817 --> 20:09.385
<i>♪ When you least expect you'll
find magic in your life ♪</i>

20:09.420 --> 20:11.420
What the...?
What the hell is this?

20:11.456 --> 20:13.923
Oh, in India it's
traditional to do a final

20:13.958 --> 20:16.993
musical curtain call
over the end credits.

20:17.028 --> 20:20.463
<i>♪ Brian came so far,
but he never found a wife ♪</i>

20:20.498 --> 20:22.131
<i>♪ Ho-ho ♪</i>

20:22.167 --> 20:24.033
<i>♪ Big show ♪</i>

20:24.068 --> 20:25.735
<i>♪ Ho-ho ♪</i>

20:25.770 --> 20:27.303
<i>♪ Time to go ♪</i>

20:27.338 --> 20:28.571
This is kind of weird.

20:28.606 --> 20:30.673
Come on, Brian,
just surrender to it.

20:30.708 --> 20:32.642
Hey, I was in the episode, too!

20:32.677 --> 20:34.744
♪ Bing-go! ♪

20:34.779 --> 20:36.145
♪ And I'm Joe ♪

20:36.181 --> 20:37.446
Joe is the captain again!

20:37.482 --> 20:40.349
All right, I'll give it a shot.

20:40.385 --> 20:42.218
♪ Well, I came
across the world ♪

20:42.253 --> 20:44.120
♪ For a very special girl... ♪

20:49.260 --> 20:50.993
Eyes forward,
finish the number.

20:51.029 --> 20:53.029
Ranita, finish the number!

20:54.985 --> 22:01.485
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru